1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,850
In Spain the appointment is ten minutes and the paperwork is a folder.

2
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:08,850
Some of it is unreadable. Guessing is worse.

3
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:13,850
Anteroom turns that folder into one structured brief.

4
00:00:14,150 --> 00:00:20,850
Photograph the paperwork, or pick it from the library.

5
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:26,850
They upload to your account, and you can see exactly what you captured.

6
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:33,850
Gemini Flash types the document. You can override it in one tap.

7
00:00:34,150 --> 00:00:38,850
Gemini 2.5 Pro reads both pages, in the EU.

8
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:43,850
Eighteen seconds later, the brief is there.

9
00:00:44,150 --> 00:00:50,850
It found seven medications. And it refused to guess the eighth.

10
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:56,850
Every other drug has its dose, verbatim. Warfarin has none.

11
00:00:57,150 --> 00:01:01,850
And the original page is one tap away, so any line can be checked.

12
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:07,850
Export a PDF for the clinic. On the free tier the server watermarks it.

13
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:12,850
Pro removes the watermark and renders it in Spanish.

14
00:01:13,150 --> 00:01:17,850
RevenueCat purchases-kmp — one implementation, two stores.

15
00:01:18,150 --> 00:01:22,850
The server decides, not the client. It cannot unlock itself.

16
00:01:23,150 --> 00:01:30,850
Android, iOS, desktop and web — from one Kotlin codebase.
